CI caught this on the config-store PR: every hypergumbo self-claim dropped from
confirmed_with_caveats to inconclusive, three of them flagged REGRESSED on
credited_flows. A/B on a clean dev tree confirmed the cause was mine, not
pre-existing (dev: "OK - 18 claims unchanged").

MECHANISM, traced rather than guessed. BoundaryCoverage.qualifying_only is
`not unknown`, so the uncatalogued-module list must be EXACTLY EMPTY for an
opaque launch to QUALIFY a verdict rather than withhold it. The new config
loader imports tomllib; _uncatalogued_external_modules reported it; `unknown`
became non-empty; qualifying_only flipped False; and the taint qualifier's
`if opaque_sites:` branch fell through to inconclusive for all 18. The verdict
TEXT still named only the opaque launches, which is why the drift looked
unrelated to the change that caused it.

THE GATE IS RIGHT AND WAS NOT WIDENED. This is INV-buzab's distinction working
as designed: is_stdlib_module recognises the NAME (tomllib was already in
stdlib_modules) while module_io_is_enumerated is the predicate that vouches for
the silence, and 283 of Python's 300 enumerated stdlib modules carry no rows.
Treating recognition as examination is exactly what confirmed "never sends data
over the network" for a program writing a secret into telnetlib.Telnet. So the
fix is a POSITIVE DATED DECLARATION, per the standing rule.

VERDICT AND EVIDENCE for the declaration. tomllib.load(fp) reads from a binary
file OBJECT the caller opened and loads(s) is pure string parsing, so the open
is the caller's I/O and is rowed where it happens — the same shape as json,
declared beside it. The survey probe (docs/surveys/python-stdlib-module-io-
enumeration.md) was re-run on 2026-08-23: public API is load/loads/
TOMLDecodeError, and the sole `open(` match anywhere in tomllib._parser is
inside the TypeError text "File must be opened in binary mode, e.g. use
`open('foo.toml', 'rb')`" — the docstring/message false-positive class that
survey already documents, not a call.

THE LEVERAGE IS THE POINT, not an accident: the self-proof sits on a knife edge
by construction, and one unaudited import takes it off. The honest response is
to audit the module. Recorded as a dated addendum on the survey, which also
flags its own 2026-08-15 line "the 18 claims remain inconclusive" as historical
— later work drove the count to zero, which is why one call could move
everything.

